    {
      "id": "upload",
      "label": "Upload it as a variant",
      "state": "not-run-for-this-entry",
      "summary": "The Catalog has not uploaded this entry. The commands use its signed installer package.",
      "basis": [
        "source.ociRef",
        "oci.bundles[literal-config]",
        "oci.bundles[confighub-upload]",
        "oci.bundles[confighub-release]",
        "lifecycle.coverage.confighub_scan_ops"
      ],
      "commands": [
        {
          "comment": "sign in; steps 3 to 5 write to your ConfigHub organization",
          "command": "cub auth login",
          "needsAccount": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "put the signed package into a Space in one command: it pulls, renders and uploads",
          "command": "cub package install oci://ghcr.io/confighub/packages/argo-cd-helm:v10.20.0@sha256:c2b3d56b46a6cf53a09ccec757755f31a3060ac0549fdd1af4b9bec2ab6f0f29 --base default --space <your-space> --namespace argocd --non-interactive",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "or, to name the Component yourself, upload step 1's directory instead",
          "command": "cub installer upload --work-dir ./argo-cd-argo-cd-10-20-0-default --space <your-space> --component <your-component>",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "list the Units the upload created",
          "command": "cub unit list --space <your-space>",
          "needsAccount": true
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Replace each value in angle brackets with a name of your own. The entry id may already exist as a Space in your organization, and the package name as a Component.",
        "`cub package install` names the Component after the package. To choose its name, run step 1's `cub installer setup` and then `cub installer upload` with `--component`. In the run of 2026-11-26 for the nginx entry, both forms created the same Units.",
        "In the walk of 2026-10-08, a Space named for the nginx entry's id and a Component named bitnami-nginx already existed, so the walk chose its own names.",
        "The cub installer plugin reads your organization from `CUB_CONTEXT` and ignores `--context`. If you use a context other than your default, export `CUB_CONTEXT` first, or the plugin works in your default organization."
      ],
      "liveWalk": {
        "date": "2026-11-26",
        "path": "docs/user/live-walk-cub-package-install-2026-11-26.md",
        "url": "https://github.com/confighub/helm-expt/blob/main/docs/user/live-walk-cub-package-install-2026-11-26.md",
        "versions": "cub v0.11.23, ConfigHub server v0.11.1 and installer plugin 0.6.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "deploy",
      "label": "Deploy it",
      "state": "not-run-for-this-entry",
      "summary": "No delivery run is recorded for this entry. Argo CD has not run, Flux has not run, and kubectl has not run.",
      "basis": [
        "oci.runtimes",
        "lifecycle.installTimeInputs"
      ],
      "commands": [
        {
          "comment": "clone the base onto a Target as a dev variant",
          "command": "cub variant create dev <your-space> --target workshop/target --space-pattern \"template:<your-space>-dev\"",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "publish the Release that the cluster's Argo CD pulls",
          "command": "cub release publish <your-space>-dev",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Use the Space name you chose in step 3. The upload also keeps a record of the package as a hidden Unit named `installer`. The variant does not clone it, so one publish deploys the rendered objects.",
        "ConfigHub shows nothing when Argo CD fails to read a Release. Run `kubectl -n argocd get applications.argoproj.io` and read the Sync column, because Healthy alone is not a pass. In the walk, the Application was Synced and Healthy about 4.5 minutes after the publish, on a cluster made without k8sbot.",
        "Make the cluster with `cub cluster up --name workshop --no-k8sbot`. That command creates two Spaces, a Target, a service account and a Trigger, opens ten ports on the machine, and installs Argo CD from an unpinned upstream manifest. Argo CD in the cluster pulls each Release from the ConfigHub server, so the cluster has to reach it."
      ],
      "liveWalk": {
        "date": "2026-11-27",
        "path": "docs/user/live-walk-entry-deploy-promote-2026-11-27.md",
        "url": "https://github.com/confighub/helm-expt/blob/main/docs/user/live-walk-entry-deploy-promote-2026-11-27.md",
        "versions": "cub v0.11.23, ConfigHub server v0.11.1, installer plugin 0.6.1 and kind v0.31.0"
      },
      "needs": [
        "argocd-redis"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "promote",
      "label": "Promote a change",
      "state": "not-run-for-this-entry",
      "summary": "No promotion is recorded for this entry.",
      "basis": [
        "lifecycle.promotion"
      ],
      "commands": [
        {
          "comment": "preview what the dev variant would take from the base",
          "command": "cub variant promote <your-space>-dev --dry-run -o mutations",
          "needsAccount": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "promote once you have read the preview",
          "command": "cub variant promote <your-space>-dev --change-desc \"Pull the reviewed base forward\"",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "publish the Release that carries the change",
          "command": "cub release publish <your-space>-dev",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The promotion changes the dev Space and publishes nothing. The change reaches the cluster only after the publish. The promotion also adds the hidden `installer` Unit to the dev Space, without a Target, and the Release leaves it out.",
        "The preview lists the whole installer record as added. In the walk, the preview of a one-field change to nginx ran to 57 lines, and about 50 of them were that record."
      ],
      "liveWalk": {
        "date": "2026-11-27",
        "path": "docs/user/live-walk-entry-deploy-promote-2026-11-27.md",
        "url": "https://github.com/confighub/helm-expt/blob/main/docs/user/live-walk-entry-deploy-promote-2026-11-27.md",
        "versions": "cub v0.11.23, ConfigHub server v0.11.1, installer plugin 0.6.1 and kind v0.31.0"
      }
    }
